{"skill":{"slug":"tavily-search-1-0-0","displayName":"Tavily Search 1.0.0"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771074878552,"changelog":"Initial release of Tavily Search skill.\n\n- Provides AI-optimized web search via the Tavily API, designed for AI agents.\n- Supports search with options for number of results, deep search, topic selection (general/news), and date filtering for news.\n- Allows extracting clean content from specific URLs.\n- Requires a TAVILY_API_KEY for operation.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1195,"sha256":"c1c4f168eb62dc1b3b3da18186963419b5fac7f9e62c098c0ce3ace482060c7d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":132,"sha256":"ba35afebbdb2aebb0c204c923da17b154d9dd11fd3fd2a02117f2a171086d3b4","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/extract.mjs","size":1336,"sha256":"89c80e4584a623b858c72315a619227b093c2b2b3bac809788b6f9b0a9e2fd31","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/search.mjs","size":2299,"sha256":"226d73a4b9b9a45390f9f7b6be6c7a0b46c8deb1a0cbf3f825b7fadc23259f3f","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1791,"sha256":"1a7745170aa1bf33583578f0d03947de5513ca8c54730993cce8da76c270e195","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789067377345,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a77ac1030874dcfd4c105d123c791dc5005ede5c253b2aa3c8103b95544d80d4","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a77ac1030874dcfd4c105d123c791dc5005ede5c253b2aa3c8103b95544d80d4","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: tavily-search-1-0-0\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides a straightforward wrapper for the Tavily API, enabling web search and content extraction. It reads the `TAVILY_API_KEY` from environment variables and makes legitimate API calls to `https://api.tavily.com` as intended. There is no evidence of data exfiltration beyond the necessary API key for the service, no malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the agent in `SKILL.md`. The scripts `scripts/extract.mjs` and `scripts/search.mjs` correctly parse command-line arguments and interact with the specified external API.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163982696},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":58,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789067377345},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward Tavily web search and URL extraction wrapper with disclosed API key and network use, and I found no hidden persistence, privilege escalation, or unrelated behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill requires Node and TAVILY_API_KEY, then sends search queries or requested URLs to api.tavily.com, which is proportionate for a Tavily integration.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No installer, dependency installation, postinstall hook, or remote code execution mechanism is present in the inspected artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The extract command accepts user-supplied URLs and sends them to Tavily; this is documented, but users should avoid passing private, internal, or sensitive URLs.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The scripts do not write files, modify system settings, create background services, access local credential stores, or persist across runs.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Tavily-powered web search, and the documented commands perform Tavily search plus explicitly documented URL content extraction.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending search queries and any extracted URLs to Tavily under your Tavily account. Do not use the extract command on confidential, internal, localhost, or otherwise sensitive URLs unless that disclosure is acceptable.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The skill does use Node, outbound network access, and TAVILY_API_KEY, but those requirements are declared in the skill metadata and fit the Tavily API wrapper purpose.\n[SDI-2] expected: The arbitrary URL extraction capability is broader than the short metadata description alone, but SKILL.md has a dedicated 'Extract content from URL' section showing the exact command.\n[E1] expected: External POST requests to Tavily search and extract endpoints are the core function of the skill; I found no additional destinations or unrelated transmissions.\n[SDI-1] expected: The extract endpoint returns raw page content for user-provided URLs, which is a documented feature of this skill rather than hidden behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: The scripts send the API key and user query or URL to Tavily without a separate runtime confirmation, but the requirement for TAVILY_API_KEY and the Tavily service dependency are disclosed.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789067377345}}}}}